## 🚨 Common Pitfalls & Solutions

### CSS @css Placement Error

```dart
// ❌ WRONG - Will cause compilation errors
class MyComponent extends StatefulComponent {
  @override
  State<MyComponent> createState() => _MyComponentState();
}

class _MyComponentState extends State<MyComponent> {
  @css  // ERROR: Can't use @css on private _State class
  static List<StyleRule> get styles => [...];
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Move @css to public component class
class MyComponent extends StatefulComponent {
  @css  // CORRECT: @css on public component class
  static List<StyleRule> get styles => [...];

  @override
  State<MyComponent> createState() => _MyComponentState();
}

class _MyComponentState extends State<MyComponent> {
  // No @css here, styles are defined in the public class
}
```

### Server/Client Rendering Issues

```dart
// ❌ WRONG - Causes frame scheduling errors
class MyService extends ChangeNotifier {
  void updateData() {
    data = newData;
    notifyListeners(); // ERROR: Causes frame scheduling error on server
  }
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Conditional notification
class MyService extends ChangeNotifier {
  void updateData() {
    data = newData;
    if (kIsWeb) notifyListeners(); // SAFE: Only notify on client
  }
}
```

### Import Management After Refactoring

```dart
// ✅ SYSTEMATIC APPROACH to fixing imports after refactoring

// 1. Update the component that changed
// 2. Use IDE's "Find All References"
// 3. Update imports in this order:
//    - Direct imports first
//    - Transitive dependencies second
//    - Test files last

// Example: After moving ProjectCard to accept ProjectModel:
// OLD: import '../molecules/project_card.dart'; // Still works
// NEW: import '../models/project_model.dart';   // Now also needed
```

## 📋 Debugging Checklist

When things go wrong:

1. **CSS not applying?**

   - Check if `.styles(raw: const {...})` is used correctly
   - Verify type wrappers: `ZIndex(n)`, `lineHeight.px`
   - Ensure `@css` is on public class, not private `_State`

2. **Component not updating?**

   - Check if `kIsWeb` guards are around `notifyListeners()`
   - Verify `ListenableBuilder` is used on client side
   - Ensure server-side rendering path doesn't use reactive builders

3. **Linter errors after refactoring?**

   - Fix imports systematically
   - Update component APIs one at a time
   - Use find-all-references before changing APIs

4. **Assets not loading?**
   - Verify files are in `web/` directory
   - Check path starts with `/` (absolute from web root)
   - Ensure build process includes the assets
